{
  "id": 236748373,
  "iid": 11427,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "PROXYv2: support coalesced packets",
  "description": "Call next dissector when there is data remaining after dissection the same way PROXYv1 dissector does\n\nCloses #19208 \n\n---\n\nThis implementation has the same restrictions as PROXYv1 (e.g. broken in a two pass dissection like when coalesced with HTTP), but at least it is able to dissect other cases in the same way PROXYv1 does (like the one in the original issue).  \n\nHere's a sample pcapng dump with different test cases:\n- PROXYv2 only\n- PROXYv2 + SMPP PDU in a single segment\n- PROXYv2 + SMPP PDU in two segments (reassembly)\n\n[proxyv2-smpp-test.pcapng](/uploads/4ae78917b935a1cd64b8e8c3218fea53/proxyv2-smpp-test.pcapng)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-07-15T09:45:07.998Z",
